 "prop:intersectionsubset": {
  "id": "prop:intersectionsubset",
  "kind": "Proposition",
  "number": 8,
  "page": "12-intersections.html",
  "title": "an intersection is a subset of each set",
  "statement": "For any sets <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span>, <span class='m'><i>X</i> ∩ <i>Y</i> ⊂ <i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>X</i> ∩ <i>Y</i> ⊂ <i>Y</i></span>.",
  "proof": "<p>Let <span class='m'><i>x</i></span> be an arbitrary element of <span class='m'><i>X</i> ∩ <i>Y</i></span>.\n\tBy the definition of intersection, <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>Y</i></span>.\n\tHence every element of <span class='m'><i>X</i> ∩ <i>Y</i></span> is an element of both <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span>.</p>",
  "figure": ""
 },
