 "prop:unionsubset": {
  "id": "prop:unionsubset",
  "kind": "Proposition",
  "number": 15,
  "page": "13-unions.html",
  "title": "each set is a subset of the union",
  "statement": "For any sets <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span>, <span class='m'><i>X</i> ⊂ <i>X</i> ∪ <i>Y</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i> ⊂ <i>X</i> ∪ <i>Y</i></span>.",
  "proof": "<p>Suppose <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i></span>.\n\tThen we immediately have <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i></span> or <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>Y</i></span>; hence <span class='m'><i>x</i></span> satisfies the inclusion criterion for <span class='m'><i>X</i> ∪ <i>Y</i></span>; hence <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i> ∪ <i>Y</i></span>.\n\tSince <span class='m'><i>x</i></span> was chosen arbitrarily, it follows that <span class='m'><i>X</i> ⊂ <i>X</i> ∪ <i>Y</i></span>.</p><p>The proof that <span class='m'><i>Y</i> ⊂ <i>X</i> ∪ <i>Y</i></span> is exactly analogous.</p>",
  "figure": ""
 },
 "prop:unioncommutes": {
  "id": "prop:unioncommutes",
  "kind": "Proposition",
  "number": 16,
  "page": "13-unions.html",
  "title": "union commutes",
  "statement": "For any sets <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span>, <span class='m'><i>X</i> ∪ <i>Y</i> = <i>Y</i> ∪ <i>X</i></span>.",
  "proof": "",
  "figure": ""
 },
