 "prop:contraposition": {
  "id": "prop:contraposition",
  "kind": "Proposition",
  "number": 38,
  "page": "16-complements.html",
  "title": "complements reverse inclusion",
  "statement": "<span class='m'><i>X</i> ⊂ <i>Y</i></span> if and only if <span class='m'><i>Y</i><sup><i>c</i></sup> ⊂ <i>X</i><sup><i>c</i></sup></span>.",
  "proof": "<p>Left to right: suppose that <span class='m'><i>X</i> ⊂ <i>Y</i></span>.\n\tIf it were not the case that <span class='m'><i>Y</i><sup><i>c</i></sup> ⊂ <i>X</i><sup><i>c</i></sup></span>, then there would be some <span class='m'><i>x</i></span> which belongs to <span class='m'><i>Y</i><sup><i>c</i></sup></span> but not to <span class='m'><i>X</i><sup><i>c</i></sup></span>.\n\tIn that case, we would have <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i></span> but <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∉ <i>Y</i></span>, contradicting that <span class='m'><i>X</i> ⊂ <i>Y</i></span>.</p><p>Right to left: this follows from the previous step of the argument if we apply <a class='xref' data-ref='prop:doublecomplement' href='16-complements.html#prop:doublecomplement' title='Proposition 32 (the complement of a complement)'>Proposition&nbsp;32&nbsp;(the complement of a complement)</a>. (Do you see why?)</p>",
  "figure": "<figure class='block fig' id='fig:contraposition' data-ref='fig:contraposition' data-open='1'><div class='figbody' data-toggle><div class='pic'><svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 72.4 42.4' role='img' class='figsvg'><defs><pattern id='contraposition-hNE' width='1.3' height='1.3' patternUnits='userSpaceOnUse'><path d='M 0 1.3 L 1.3 0' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='0.15'/></pattern><pattern id='contraposition-hNW' width='1.3' height='1.3' patternUnits='userSpaceOnUse'><path d='M 0 0 L 1.3 1.3' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='0.15'/></pattern><mask id='contraposition-m0' maskUnits='userSpaceOnUse' x='0' y='0' width='72.4' height='42.4'><rect x='0' y='0' width='72.4' height='42.4' fill='#fff'/><path d='M 23.2 21.2 a 8.0 8.0 0 1 0 16.0 0 a 8.0 8.0 0 1 0 -16.0 0 Z' fill='#000'/></mask><clipPath id='contraposition-c1'><path d='M 1.2 1.2 h 70.0 v 40.0 h -70.0 Z'/></clipPath><mask id='contraposition-m2' maskUnits='userSpaceOnUse' x='0' y='0' width='72.4' height='42.4'><rect x='0' y='0' width='72.4' height='42.4' fill='#fff'/><path d='M 19.200000000000003 21.2 a 15.0 15.0 0 1 0 30.0 0 a 15.0 15.0 0 1 0 -30.0 0 Z' fill='#000'/></mask><clipPath id='contraposition-c3'><path d='M 1.2 1.2 h 70.0 v 40.0 h -70.0 Z'/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path='url(#contraposition-c1)'><g mask='url(#contraposition-m0)'><rect x='0' y='0' width='72.4' height='42.4' fill='url(#contraposition-hNE)'/></g></g><g clip-path='url(#contraposition-c3)'><g mask='url(#contraposition-m2)'><rect x='0' y='0' width='72.4' height='42.4' fill='url(#contraposition-hNW)'/></g></g><path d='M 1.2 1.2 h 70.0 v 40.0 h -70.0 Z' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='0.18'/><path d='M 19.200000000000003 21.2 a 15.0 15.0 0 1 0 30.0 0 a 15.0 15.0 0 1 0 -30.0 0 Z' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='0.18'/><path d='M 23.2 21.2 a 8.0 8.0 0 1 0 16.0 0 a 8.0 8.0 0 1 0 -16.0 0 Z' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='0.18'/><text x='31.2' y='21.2' font-size='2.35' text-anchor='middle' dominant-baseline='central' font-family='Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif' font-style='italic' fill='currentColor'>X</text><text x='44.2' y='21.2' font-size='2.35' text-anchor='middle' dominant-baseline='central' font-family='Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif' font-style='italic' stroke='var(--fig-bg, #fff)' stroke-width='1.55' stroke-linejoin='round' paint-order='stroke' fill='currentColor'>Y</text><text x='6.2' y='6.2' font-size='2.35' text-anchor='middle' dominant-baseline='central' font-family='Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif' font-style='italic' stroke='var(--fig-bg, #fff)' stroke-width='1.55' stroke-linejoin='round' paint-order='stroke' fill='currentColor'>U</text></svg></div></div><figcaption><span class='lbl' data-toggle>Figure 17.</span> <a class='xref' data-ref='prop:contraposition' href='16-complements.html#prop:contraposition' title='Proposition 38 (complements reverse inclusion)'>Proposition&nbsp;38&nbsp;(complements reverse inclusion)</a>: complements reverse inclusion.</figcaption></figure>"
 },
 "def:disjoint": {
  "id": "def:disjoint",
  "kind": "Definition",
  "number": 12,
  "page": "17-disjointness.html",
  "title": "Disjoint",
  "statement": "<span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span> are <em>disjoint</em> when <span class='m'><i>X</i> ∩ <i>Y</i> = ∅</span>.",
  "proof": "",
  "figure": ""
 },
 "prop:disjointdifference": {
  "id": "prop:disjointdifference",
  "kind": "Proposition",
  "number": 39,
  "page": "17-disjointness.html",
  "title": "a set is disjoint from what is taken off another",
  "statement": "For any sets <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span>, <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i></span> are disjoint.",
  "proof": "<p>Suppose for contradiction that there is some <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i> ∩ (<i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i>)</span>.\n\tThen we have <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i></span> by the definition of intersection and <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∉ <i>X</i></span> by the definition of intersection and relative complement.\n\tThese two statements are contradictory.</p>",
  "figure": ""
 },
 "prop:disjointsubset": {
  "id": "prop:disjointsubset",
  "kind": "Proposition",
  "number": 40,
  "page": "17-disjointness.html",
  "title": "disjointness passes to subsets",
  "statement": "For any sets <span class='m'><i>X</i></span>, <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Z</i></span>, if <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span> are disjoint and <span class='m'><i>Z</i> ⊂ <i>X</i></span>, then <span class='m'><i>Z</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span> are disjoint.",
  "proof": "<p>Suppose that <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span> are disjoint and that <span class='m'><i>Z</i> ⊂ <i>X</i></span>.\n\tSince <span class='m'><i>Z</i> ⊂ <i>X</i></span>, <a class='xref' data-ref='prop:intersectionmonotone' href='12-intersections.html#prop:intersectionmonotone' title='Proposition 9 (intersection respects inclusion)'>Proposition&nbsp;9&nbsp;(intersection respects inclusion)</a> gives us <span class='m'><i>Z</i> ∩ <i>Y</i> ⊂ <i>X</i> ∩ <i>Y</i></span>.\n\tBut <span class='m'><i>X</i> ∩ <i>Y</i> = ∅</span>, since <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span> are disjoint, so <span class='m'><i>Z</i> ∩ <i>Y</i> ⊂ ∅</span>.\n\tBy <a class='xref' data-ref='prop:subsetofempty' href='10-the-empty-set.html#prop:subsetofempty' title='Proposition 6 (the only subset of ∅)'>Proposition&nbsp;6&nbsp;(the only subset of ∅)</a>, then, <span class='m'><i>Z</i> ∩ <i>Y</i> = ∅</span>; that is, <span class='m'><i>Z</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span> are disjoint.</p>",
  "figure": ""
 },
