 "prop:disjointdecomposition": {
  "id": "prop:disjointdecomposition",
  "kind": "Proposition",
  "number": 41,
  "page": "17-disjointness.html",
  "title": "splitting a set around a subset",
  "statement": "For any sets <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span>, if <span class='m'><i>X</i> ⊂ <i>Y</i></span>, then <span class='m'><i>Y</i> = <i>X</i> ∪ (<i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i>)</span>.",
  "proof": "<p>Suppose that <span class='m'><i>X</i> ⊂ <i>Y</i></span>.\n\tWe will show that <span class='m'><i>Y</i> = <i>X</i> ∪ (<i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i>)</span> using <a class='xref' data-ref='prop:doubleinclusion' href='08-subsets.html#prop:doubleinclusion' title='Proposition 1 (double inclusion)'>Proposition&nbsp;1&nbsp;(double inclusion)</a>.</p><p>First, let us show that <span class='m'><i>Y</i> ⊂ <i>X</i> ∪ (<i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i>)</span>.\n\tLet <span class='m'><i>y</i> ∈ <i>Y</i></span>.\n\tBy the law of excluded middle, either (i) <span class='m'><i>y</i> ∈ <i>X</i></span> or (ii) <span class='m'><i>y</i> ∉ <i>X</i></span>.\n\tCase (i): if <span class='m'><i>y</i> ∈ <i>X</i></span>, then <span class='m'><i>y</i> ∈ <i>X</i> ∪ (<i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i>)</span> by the definition of union.\n\tCase (ii): if <span class='m'><i>y</i> ∉ <i>X</i></span>, then <span class='m'><i>y</i> ∈ <i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i></span> by the definition of relative complement; hence <span class='m'><i>y</i> ∈ <i>X</i> ∪ (<i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i>)</span> by the definition of union.</p><p>Next we will show that <span class='m'><i>X</i> ∪ (<i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i>) ⊂ <i>Y</i></span>.\n\tSuppose that <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i> ∪ (<i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i>)</span>.\n\tThere are two cases: either (i) <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i></span> or (ii) <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i></span>.\n\tCase (i): if <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>X</i></span>, then since <span class='m'><i>X</i> ⊂ <i>Y</i></span> we have <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>Y</i></span>.\n\tCase (ii): if <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i></span>, then by definition of relative complement, <span class='m'><i>x</i> ∈ <i>Y</i></span>.</p>",
  "figure": "<figure class='block fig' id='fig:disjointdecomposition' data-ref='fig:disjointdecomposition' data-open='1'><div class='figbody' data-toggle><div class='pic'><svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 38.9 38.4' role='img' class='figsvg'><defs><pattern id='disjointdecomposition-hNE' width='1.3' height='1.3' patternUnits='userSpaceOnUse'><path d='M 0 1.3 L 1.3 0' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='0.15'/></pattern><pattern id='disjointdecomposition-hNW' width='1.3' height='1.3' patternUnits='userSpaceOnUse'><path d='M 0 0 L 1.3 1.3' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='0.15'/></pattern><mask id='disjointdecomposition-m0' maskUnits='userSpaceOnUse' x='0' y='0' width='38.9' height='38.4'><rect x='0' y='0' width='38.9' height='38.4' fill='#fff'/><path d='M 5.199999999999999 19.2 a 9.0 9.0 0 1 0 18.0 0 a 9.0 9.0 0 1 0 -18.0 0 Z' fill='#000'/></mask><clipPath id='disjointdecomposition-c1'><path d='M 1.1999999999999993 19.2 a 18.0 18.0 0 1 0 36.0 0 a 18.0 18.0 0 1 0 -36.0 0 Z'/></clipPath><clipPath id='disjointdecomposition-c2'><path d='M 5.199999999999999 19.2 a 9.0 9.0 0 1 0 18.0 0 a 9.0 9.0 0 1 0 -18.0 0 Z'/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path='url(#disjointdecomposition-c1)'><g mask='url(#disjointdecomposition-m0)'><rect x='0' y='0' width='38.9' height='38.4' fill='url(#disjointdecomposition-hNW)'/></g></g><g clip-path='url(#disjointdecomposition-c2)'><rect x='0' y='0' width='38.9' height='38.4' fill='url(#disjointdecomposition-hNE)'/></g><path d='M 1.1999999999999993 19.2 a 18.0 18.0 0 1 0 36.0 0 a 18.0 18.0 0 1 0 -36.0 0 Z' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='0.18'/><path d='M 5.199999999999999 19.2 a 9.0 9.0 0 1 0 18.0 0 a 9.0 9.0 0 1 0 -18.0 0 Z' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='0.18'/><text x='14.2' y='19.2' font-size='2.35' text-anchor='middle' dominant-baseline='central' font-family='Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif' font-style='italic' stroke='var(--fig-bg, #fff)' stroke-width='1.55' stroke-linejoin='round' paint-order='stroke' fill='currentColor'>X</text><text x='30.2' y='19.2' font-size='2.35' text-anchor='middle' dominant-baseline='central' font-family='Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif' font-style='italic' stroke='var(--fig-bg, #fff)' stroke-width='1.55' stroke-linejoin='round' paint-order='stroke' fill='currentColor'>Y ∖ X</text></svg></div></div><figcaption><span class='lbl' data-toggle>Figure 18.</span> <a class='xref' data-ref='prop:disjointdecomposition' href='17-disjointness.html#prop:disjointdecomposition' title='Proposition 41 (splitting a set around a subset)'>Proposition&nbsp;41&nbsp;(splitting a set around a subset)</a>: <span class='m'><i>Y</i></span> split into <span class='m'><i>X</i></span> and <span class='m'><i>Y</i> ∖ <i>X</i></span>.</figcaption></figure>"
 },
